In this example : 

``` php
<?php
namespace app\assets;

use yii\web\AssetBundle;

class FontAwesomeAsset extends AssetBundle 
{
    public $sourcePath = '@bower/font-awesome'; 
    public $css = [ 
        'css/font-awesome.min.css', 
    ];
    public $publishOptions = [
        'only' => [
            'fonts/',
            'css/',
        ]
    ];
} 
```

Assets not publish files : 

![screenshot_2](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/6630197/10272919/d8f00080-6b27-11e5-904a-29b6de2661d9.png)

Hi everybody I tried to publish font awesome asset with the "only" option set to "css/" and "fonts/" like so:

```
<?php
namespace app\assets;
use yii\web\AssetBundle;

class FontAwesomeAsset extends AssetBundle
{
    // The files are not web directory accessible, therefore we need 
    // to specify the sourcePath property. Notice the @vendor alias used.
    public $sourcePath = '@vendor/components/font-awesome';
    public $css = [
        'css/font-awesome.css',
    ];
    public $publishOptions = [
        'only' => [
            'fonts/',
            'css/',
        ]
    ];
}
```

But when the asset is published, those folders (css & fonts) are empty.
On the other hand, when I tried to use the "except" option like so:

```
<?php

namespace app\assets;
use yii\web\AssetBundle;

class FontAwesomeAsset extends AssetBundle
{
    // The files are not web directory accessible, therefore we need 
    // to specify the sourcePath property. Notice the @vendor alias used.
    public $sourcePath = '@vendor/components/font-awesome';
    public $css = [
        'css/font-awesome.css',
    ];
    public $publishOptions = [
        'except' => [
            'less/',
            'scss/',
        ]
    ];
}
```

It actually worked (i.e., css and fonts folders where the only one published with their contents)
